  "term": "DSM–IV–TR",
  "definition": "DSM-IV-TR is the fourth edition, text revision, of the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, a manual used to define mental disorder diagnoses. In the source, it is identified as the version before DSM-5 and is noted for using an ADHD onset rule requiring some impairing symptoms to be present before age 7.",
